Subject: [Backport Wine 11.0] dsound: Optimize resampling with upstream SSE kernels.
Base: Wine 11.0, db11d0fe6a169c457e23d007e20404643d067aa8
Upstream: https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/commit/61e1bac10fc85a527e0fa200f409de55f723f238

Combined backport of the 32 selected upstream commits listed below. Includes
FIR filter, coefficient reuse, arithmetic and table-layout prerequisites, then
SSE upsampling and downsampling. Excludes unrelated device lifetime, surround,
denormal-control and volume changes. No Boxedwine host audio hook is needed.
Wine 11.21 already contains these changes; apply this backport only to 11.0.

The diff payload is identical to the tested guest Wine backport:
SHA-256 c17edef3fca890fe3c749424777616d37f59f9818092c147af553cd0943da17a
Retains Wine's LGPL-2.1-or-later licensing and source copyright notices.

Selected upstream commits, in order (wine-mirror/wine):
e33cf2c07bea270f2b170835e5a52180c09f93ea dsound: Use a better FIR filter generated with the Parks-McClellan algorithm.
e023741de82bf22538c72c9e2bde559726ef867d dsound: Remove the unused freqneeded field.
0e83f60183ce6939ba154f1cab6cb33747d2da67 dsound: Don't use double-precision arithmetic in the resampler.
ae384834809eb26b22acd8eb5de3d4a4c1798f5d dsound: Do the subtraction before converting to float to improve rem precision.
9f9cb2f96b660beb9bb3d2a00421a464e4b39f0e dsound: Use the modulus operator instead of divide-multiply-subtract.
027ba3f95e3e25b178bddb9c0e236ec7496d7dc8 dsound: Multiply by dsbfirstep after calculating the modulus.
47fb02fe5a7eab05b225ef3b44fd8dc608bafdb8 dsound: Get rid of fir_copy.
a1ac7b73c08873f7625b56a078e52ebc9ef314f2 dsound: Resample one channel at a time.
978318c3f5e581b3744311352452ca922451c39b dsound: Resample into a temporary buffer.
5c19fed232f4e399ec337e641dcc7dc16dc5c5e0 dsound: Remove asserts from the resampling loop.
b261e4d7c46355c59d1e1527825a80a8a9612221 dsound: Factor out resampling.
075b7d84027a6ae578f794bfdf87717e1e686436 dsound: Split resample into separate downsample and upsample functions.
3719498d54f5f52809e804048a5b6ed69baf3bc4 dsound: Don't apply firgain in upsample.
f797d0418e9bbf7919ff0bb488995012456222d3 dsound: Don't pass dsbfirstep to upsample.
68466e2dbf338e3df4eb9b8e4cdd990a628eaae3 dsound: Use a fixed upsampling loop boundary.
e788b95dda4c3b1bfcbcbe66782be4b84370fa77 dsound: Don't invert the remainder twice in upsample.
82c238d4ae38c67e407a6f4d198b40a5e65a66d9 dsound: Calculate required_input more accurately.
97f3bffa60b173c43ceef6c96ed5d9a46fccef12 dsound: Swap around the two nested loops in downsample.
d0fbde08a2eb54ea4d88e61fd0f7f47fea30d463 dsound: Calculate firgain more accurately.
b54be941794df69d19e62558183110cbe1713b17 dsound: Transpose the FIR array to make the element access sequential.
217c2990c7132e3279b3b7bfe5ef0119e1495666 dsound: Premultiply the input value by firgain and the interpolation weights in downsample.
c59db3f5443b075738d260552e80d01d721e4366 dsound: Make i signed in downsample.
472c5b3dc1d8337102d306dece5821ae4ea7be9e dsound: Replace multiplications by fir_step and fir_width with bit shifts.
c195a0b8071eb9d15b360926c3bb301bcc4258fb dsound: Use a 0.32 fixed point to represent the resampling ratio.
a81c91b8ca712141e862e21239bb399ca48434bf dsound: Make rem_num signed.
f704a2d17bd333c92e636b403c69b59b58279195 dsound: Calculate opos_num and ipos_num incrementally.
b9de3e57fa3e38efe888836d6b396c0ce7c3ed00 dsound: Calculate rem and rem_inv incrementally.
d79bd1cffc06f0f724c4ae8b15c3341a5ef51bd7 dsound: Use DWORD to store freqAdjustNum, freqAdjustDen and freqAccNum.
688618ff978bdca35ffc89d0a6d8ac6bfacba9de dsound: Move cp_fields_noresample after cp_fields_resample.
3f30664a951031294c7433a03ffe8f9382f39fd9 dsound: Use #define for fir.h constants.
0dd8d009ebbb35bd5d48ea7bc659066d14077060 dsound: Add an SSE version of upsample.
61e1bac10fc85a527e0fa200f409de55f723f238 dsound: Add an SSE version of downsample.

